# Phase 11: the stdlib location must be configurable, and every command must
# agree on it.
#
# The base path used to be resolved in three places: the compiler honoured
# EZLIB_PATH, but the bundler and the package manager both hardcoded
# "C:/ezlib". So `ez run` could resolve a module from a custom EZLIB_PATH while
# `ez bundle` / `ez install` looked somewhere else. All three now go through
# ezLibBase() (src/utils/EzLibPath.h).
#
# This file is the module the harness resolves via a temporary EZLIB_PATH:
#   1. copy it to $TMP/ezlib_probe/probe.ez
#   2. EZLIB_PATH=$TMP/ezlib_probe ez test_ezlib_path_user.ez
#   3. `use "probe"` must resolve from there, not from C:/ezlib

task probeGreeting() {
    give "resolved from EZLIB_PATH"
}
